From: Aspartame GTK4 migration
Subject: [PATCH] home: let focus enter the Favorites ring

FavoritesView called set_can_focus(False) on the container that holds every
Activity icon, the owner icon and the current-activity icon. In GTK3 that only
stopped the container itself becoming a focus stop. GTK4 changed the meaning:
can-focus gates whether focus may enter the widget *or any of its children*,
so the whole ring became unreachable by keyboard. Tab on Home cycled between
the search entry and two toolbar buttons and never touched an Activity.

set_focusable(False) is the GTK4 spelling of the original intent: this widget
is not itself a focus stop, its children still are.

--- a/src/jarabe/desktop/favoritesview.py
+++ b/src/jarabe/desktop/favoritesview.py
@@ -124,7 +124,12 @@
         ViewContainer.__init__(self, layout=self._layout,
                                owner_icon=owner_icon,
                                activity_icon=current_activity)
-        self.set_can_focus(False)
+        # GTK3's set_can_focus(False) only stopped this container taking
+        # focus. In GTK4 can-focus gates whether focus may enter the widget
+        # *or any of its children*, so it made every Activity icon in the
+        # ring unreachable by keyboard. set_focusable(False) is the GTK4
+        # spelling of the original intent.
+        self.set_focusable(False)
 
         # Drag and drop is set only for the Random layout.
         self._dragging_mode = False
